# InsectSwarm preset
format = 1
name = Cricket Field
author = Ravetracer
description = Twelve crickets after dark. Not the same mechanism as a cicada, which is what 0.3.0 changed: twice the Q at 25.8, a seventh of the pulse rate at 35.9, two thirds of the time silent -- and Scrape at 0.45, because a file-and-scraper drives the harp for most of each wing stroke where a tymbal only snaps. Measured inside a chirp the references are sounding 0.27 of the time for a cricket and 0.79 for a cicada; one click into a resonator is 0.06 and is neither.
